            <ArticleTitle>Tapia syndrome caused by a vertebral artery dissection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>313-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 63-year-old man presented to our otorhinolaryngology department with hoarseness and neck pain of 3 weeks' duration. After a thorough workup, we established a diagnosis of Tapia syndrome secondary to a vertebral artery dissection. We review the literature and discuss the clinical presentation of this rare syndrome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
